From 6a42cfe4b4400812218427aeb58a41b27a896b07 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: elkir0 <elkir0@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] extcon: sm5502: VBUSIN to VBUSOUT for a USB OTG cable

For an OTG cable (ID grounded) the driver routes D+/D- to USB but leaves
the VBUSIN switch open.  On the SM5703 the charger's 5 V boost comes out
on VBUSOUT and reaches the connector only through that switch: open, the
plugged device never gets power.  Samsung's own SM5703 MUIC driver
writes MANUAL_SW1 = 0x25 for an OTG cable: D+/D- to USB and VBUSIN to
VBUSOUT.  Do the same.  A detach opens both switches, as before.

On the SM-T715, 2026-11-28: with the charger's boost on, a USB flash
disk behind an OTG adapter enumerates at high speed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/extcon/extcon-sm5502.c | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/extcon/extcon-sm5502.c b/drivers/extcon/extcon-sm5502.c
index 21a780ea1..84a6f801e 100644
--- a/drivers/extcon/extcon-sm5502.c
+++ b/drivers/extcon/extcon-sm5502.c
@@ -513,7 +513,14 @@ static int sm5502_muic_cable_handler(struct sm5502_muic_info *info,
 	case SM5502_MUIC_ADC_OPEN_USB_OTG:
 		id	= EXTCON_USB_HOST;
 		con_sw	= DM_DP_SWITCH_USB;
-		vbus_sw	= VBUSIN_SWITCH_OPEN;
+		/*
+		 * VBUSIN to VBUSOUT, as Samsung's SM5703 MUIC driver does for
+		 * an OTG cable (MANUAL_SW1 = 0x25: D+/D- to USB, VBUSIN to
+		 * VBUSOUT): the charger's 5 V boost comes out on VBUSOUT and
+		 * reaches the connector only through this switch.  Open, the
+		 * plugged device never gets power.
+		 */
+		vbus_sw	= VBUSIN_SWITCH_VBUSOUT;
 		break;
 	default:
 		dev_dbg(info->dev,
-- 
